<item>
            <title>[PARQUET-132] AvroParquetInputFormat should use a parameterized type</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-132</link>
                <project id="12315521" key="PARQUET">Parquet</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;tt&gt;AvroParquetInputFormat&lt;/tt&gt; currently extends &lt;tt&gt;ParquetInputFormat&amp;lt;IndexedRecord&amp;gt;&lt;/tt&gt;, which works for regular MR cases. But Spark&apos;s &lt;tt&gt;hadoopRDD&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://people.apache.org/~pwendell/spark-1.1.0-rc3-docs/api/java/org/apache/spark/SparkContext.html#newAPIHadoopRDD(org.apache.hadoop.conf.Configuration, java.lang.Class, java.lang.Class, java.lang.Class)&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;&lt;tt&gt;newAPIHadoopRDD&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/a&gt; methods (correctly) create a RDD with the types from the InputFormat. This means that the RDD always uses &lt;tt&gt;IndexedRecord&lt;/tt&gt; rather than the correct type.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The &lt;tt&gt;AvroParquetInputFormat&lt;/tt&gt; should be &lt;tt&gt;AvroParquetInputFormat&amp;lt;T extends IndexedRecord&amp;gt; extends ParquetInputFormat&amp;lt;T&amp;gt;&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="12755122">PARQUET-132</key>
            <summary>AvroParquetInputFormat should use a parameterized type</summary>
                <type id="1" iconUrl="https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/viewavatar?size=xsmall&amp;avatarId=21133&amp;avatarType=issuetype">Bug</type>
                                            <priority id="3" iconUrl="https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/priorities/major.svg">Major</priority>
                        <status id="5" iconUrl="https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/statuses/resolved.png" description="A resolution has been taken, and it is awaiting verification by reporter. From here issues are either reopened, or are closed.">Resolved</status>
                    <statusCategory id="3" key="done" colorName="green"/>
                                    <resolution id="1">Fixed</resolution>
                                        <assignee username="-1">Unassigned</assignee>
                                    <reporter username="rdblue">Ryan Blue</reporter>
                        <labels>
                    </labels>
                <created>Thu, 13 Nov 2014 17:57:58 +0000</created>
                <updated>Sun, 23 Jun 2024 03:27:03 +0000</updated>
                            <resolved>Wed, 19 Nov 2014 04:20:32 +0000</resolved>
                                                    <fixVersion>1.6.0</fixVersion>
                                        <due></due>
                            <votes>0</votes>
                                    <watches>3</watches>
                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="14210088" author="rdblue" created="Thu, 13 Nov 2014 18:02:05 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I&apos;ve added the change in &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-parquet-mr/pull/84&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;PR #84&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14212317" author="tomwhite" created="Fri, 14 Nov 2014 14:44:13 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;We should change it to &lt;tt&gt;AvroParquetInputFormat&amp;lt;T&amp;gt;&lt;/tt&gt; so that we can support Avro reflect in the future (see &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/Parquet/parquet-mr/pull/308&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/Parquet/parquet-mr/pull/308&lt;/a&gt;). If we changed it to &lt;tt&gt;AvroParquetInputFormat&amp;lt;T extends IndexedRecord&amp;gt;&lt;/tt&gt; then we can&apos;t at a later point change it to &lt;tt&gt;AvroParquetInputFormat&amp;lt;T&amp;gt;&lt;/tt&gt;, because adding a type parameter is compatible, while changing the bounds of one is not (see &lt;a href=&quot;https://wiki.eclipse.org/Evolving_Java-based_APIs_2#Evolving_API_Classes&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://wiki.eclipse.org/Evolving_Java-based_APIs_2#Evolving_API_Classes&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If we don&apos;t do the reflect work at this point, we could throw a runtime exception if T is not an IndexedRecord.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14212696" author="rdblue" created="Fri, 14 Nov 2014 19:31:21 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thanks for taking a look, Tom. I&apos;ve updated the PR to add &lt;tt&gt;AvroParquetInputFormat&amp;lt;T&amp;gt;&lt;/tt&gt; as you suggested. We don&apos;t actually get a reference to the type at runtime to inspect and throw an exception, so we will have to do that elsewhere. That update can wait until we add support for reflect.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14217386" author="rdblue" created="Wed, 19 Nov 2014 04:20:33 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Issue resolved by pull request 84&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-parquet-mr/pull/84&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/incubator-parquet-mr/pull/84&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17857095" author="rok" created="Sun, 23 Jun 2024 03:27:03 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This issue has been migrated to &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/parquet-java/issues/1658&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;issue #1658&lt;/a&gt; on GitHub. Please see the &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-2502&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;migration documentation&lt;/a&gt; for further details.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
